    "concept": "Binary search requires sorted input. Comparing with the midpoint discards a half that cannot contain the target; bounds must shrink on every unsuccessful step. A search interval contains every not-yet-ruled-out candidate. Sorted order enables discarding a half; an unsorted scan cannot safely use that shortcut.",
